{
  "about": "Cases of the base figures of a widget (add-small-sample-warnings, design D7, D9, D11, D13), worked out by hand with invented names and numbers, read by base-figures.spec.ts (tamiza-ui) and by BaseFiguresTests.cs (tamiza-api). The twins are base-figures.ts and BaseFigures.cs. Each case has the expected English ('en', locale en-US) and Spanish ('es', locale es-CO) texts. A case with 'apiOnly' true is for the server's twin only (the UI never writes that sentence). Sections: 'settings' (settingsInForce / BaseFigures.InForce: the widget's display and the dashboard's settings, then the settings in force), 'small' (isSmallBase / Small), 'tooltips' (figureTooltip / Tooltip: 'columns' gives the name shown for a column, 'ratio' says the widget plots the ratio of its 'numerator' to its 'denominator' columns, 'baseColumn' is the declared base column, 'figures' the numerator, denominator and n of the mark; 'lines' are [label, value] pairs), 'nLines' (nLine: the n and the name of the column it counts), 'noDataLines' (noDataLine: 'format' and 'unit' are the indicator's, or the widget's own unit), 'sentences' (the notes about small bases; 'kind' names the function and 'args' its arguments; a null expectation is a sentence that is not written).",
  "locales": { "en": "en-US", "es": "es-CO" },
